# {{.App}}

A [Beach](https://github.com/ThirdCoastInteractive/Beach) skeleton app:
SSR + Datastar over SSE, one page of driftwood components. It boots with no
database — one page, one Datastar action, one live SSE fragment.

## Run

    make up            # build + run on :8080 (or PORT=xxxx make up)

Then open http://localhost:8080/. The Tick card advances over SSE; the
Increment button mutates server state and patches the same fragment.

## Views are .templ components

All markup lives in `views.templ`. Driftwood components are called directly —
`@driftwood.Card(driftwood.CardProps{...}) { ... }` — and handlers in `main.go`
return the resulting components as `beach.View{Page: ..., Fragment: ...}`.

`templ generate` (installed as a Go tool, see go.mod) compiles `views.templ`
to `views_templ.go`. The generated file is committed, so a fresh clone builds
with plain `go build`; after editing any `.templ` file, regenerate:

    make gen           # go tool templ generate (+ css, sqlc, beach ecs gen)

Never hand-edit `*_templ.go`.

## The verification pipeline (framework doctrine)

    make gen           # templ generate + css + sqlc + beach ecs gen
    make vet           # gen, then go vet ./...
    make up            # build + run

Then a browser check: no console errors, the change is visible, no 404s. A task
is not complete until every step passes.

## Styling

The framework serves the design system from its own static tree — the
stylesheet (`/static/css/app.css`: tokens, the `dw-*` component classes), the
Datastar client, and the chart runtime. There is nothing to vendor and no
external CDN. House style: markup carries short semantic classes; long utility
strings do not belong in `.templ` files.

When the app grows custom styles, add `css/input.css` (Tailwind v4 source) —
`make css` then builds it to `static/css/{{.App}}.css` with the Tailwind CLI.

## Layout

- `main.go` — wiring only: the App, routes, the clock ticker.
- `views.templ` — all markup; `views_templ.go` is its committed compile output.
- `sqlc.yaml` — DB codegen with the `beach-apigen` plugin registered.
- `docker-compose.yml` — Postgres (ClickHouse commented out).
- `components.beach.yaml` — optional ECS component schema for `beach ecs gen`.
- `locales/` + `catalog.json` — i18n runtime + extracted catalog (`beach i18n`).

This app builds against a local Beach checkout via the `replace` directive
in `go.mod`. Point it at a published module version before shipping.
